{"id": "EUVD-2026-99014", "enisaUuid": "96371ee1-df64-34d1-b349-7f9d52540ccc", "description": "XBackBone through 3.8.2 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows authenticated users to change other users' upload share codes via the POST /upload/{id}/vanity route. Attackers can supply sequential upload ids to MediaController::createVanity() to break existing share links and hijack the freed codes with their own uploads.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:50:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T19:27:13", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sergix44/xbackbone/pull/671", "https://github.com/sergix44/xbackbone/commit/5e91a2a9859d20e41ee2e2403cfbe673804f6221", "https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/ByAj-Xoifl", "https://github.com/sergix44/xbackbone/blob/226af4f0cec218f563da6d53ececfa4708e6f3e7/app/Controllers/MediaController.php#L204-L229", "https://github.com/sergix44/xbackbone", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/xbackbone-through-3.8.2-missing-authorization-via-upload-vanity-endpoint"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110230", "GHSA-qxxw-p862-7pgx"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.31, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e127d68b-ab7c-3a11-84c6-706077535922", "product": {"name": "XBackBone", "vendor": {"name": "sergix44"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.8.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7b8cb15c-19f9-37ed-9c23-b13662f133c7", "vendor": {"name": "sergix44"}}], "isExploited": false}